                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3fc3a627-9cef-3b9c-a03a-f34d8be09e5f",
                        "entry_id": "cae01491-c326-3f5a-8fa9-508c68b42628",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To force, constrain, or obligate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37f1d371-6bd0-4f78-9e0b-843e997525c7",
                                "sense_id": "3fc3a627-9cef-3b9c-a03a-f34d8be09e5f",
                                "text": "I didn't choose to. I was compulsed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d20c5b90-3d9b-4d7d-b512-bdb51b0febe3",
                                "sense_id": "3fc3a627-9cef-3b9c-a03a-f34d8be09e5f",
                                "text": "However, a person can be more or less compulsed as it is possible for the human person to become enlightened, face and work with the particular compulsive style one as adopted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3efbddbd-9a2b-4caa-ab51-c4cc5a98f874",
                                "sense_id": "3fc3a627-9cef-3b9c-a03a-f34d8be09e5f",
                                "text": "I'm damned tired of being impressed into service, compulsed into doing things I hate to do."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "affe81c9-5be0-4852-93cc-f2105ea22f98",
                                "sense_id": "3fc3a627-9cef-3b9c-a03a-f34d8be09e5f",
                                "text": "We are compulsed to this place and put into information that is very twisted already."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ddc5bb3b-7d3d-3164-94a5-d46f1469e6cc",
                        "entry_id": "cae01491-c326-3f5a-8fa9-508c68b42628",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To behave in a compulsive manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8caa2000-942b-439f-95a3-a9bb5fb26eda",
                                "sense_id": "ddc5bb3b-7d3d-3164-94a5-d46f1469e6cc",
                                "text": "Fantasize about sex instead of obsessing and compulsing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8abd3d3a-670b-4c8c-bf18-58312b7fe958",
                                "sense_id": "ddc5bb3b-7d3d-3164-94a5-d46f1469e6cc",
                                "text": "Howard, stop talking! I asked a simple question. You gave me one of your more-than-I-will-ever- want-to-know answers. You are compulsing again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c10d5574-d228-44f8-bf77-84eec8de9eda",
                                "sense_id": "ddc5bb3b-7d3d-3164-94a5-d46f1469e6cc",
                                "text": "...where if one is not compulsing, then she is in a state of withdrawal from all activities and social interactions, as even the smallest things can trigger the obsessive fixation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
